The Optimistic Take
You don't need the full treaty to start seeing impact.

Year 2–3: A Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between 5–10 major players commits to shared CID standards, mutual peering, and pooled funding.

Year 4–5: First working prototype of a federated decentralized web—not perfect, but demonstrably interoperable.

Year 7+: The treaty becomes the formal ratification of what's already been built in practice.

